# Box art drive for the landing-page games carousel (site/demos/box-art.mjs).
# Format: <frame:int> <KeyName> <down|up>; the roguelike takes ONE turn per
# PRESSED edge, so every move is a down/up pair, spaced 10 frames apart — slow
# enough that the fog-of-war reveal and the enemy turns read as motion.
#
# The floor is fixed (seed NEON-77), so the route below is exact. The player
# spawns at (1,12) with 5 integrity; Up is -y.
#
#   x2..x5   walk the ENTRY VAULT corridor east, over the data shard at (3,12)
#   x5       two moves INTO the drone at (6,12) — moving into a hostile attacks
#            it, and it has 2 integrity, so the second one kills it
#   x6..x10  on east to the RELAY HALL, under the x=7 wall (open at y=12)
#   y11..y4  north through the y=7 wall's only door at (10,7), onto the medkit
#            at (10,4)
#   y3..y1   on north, then east along the y=1 corridor to x=15
#   (15,3)   south to the x=16 wall's door at (16,3)
#   x17,x18  east through it and three moves into the second drone at (18,3)
#
# A wall move is a wasted turn, not an error, so the tail is deliberately a
# route that stays legal all the way rather than the shortest one.
#
#   functor -d examples/roguelike run native --input-script boxart.script \
#     --script-dt 0.0166667 --capture-at-frame 60 --capture-frame /tmp/rl.png

